  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nUpper level low pressure will continue to exit the region\ntoday and be replaced by ridging and therefore quiet and warmer\nweather for the foreseeable future.\n\nThere remains strong agreement in latest global and ensemble\nguidance that ridging will keep our area free from any\nsignificant moisture sources for at least a week. In addition\nthis will aid in boosting temperatures to above normal or even\nwell above normal starting Tuesday and lasting right through \nthe weekend. Some areas could see highs in the low 60s\nWednesday-Friday. This dry stretch will continue to result in \ngrowing rainfall deficits, worsening the ongoing drought that is\nimpacting much of the region.",
